# What must NOT go into the @tm/server build context (apps/server/Dockerfile, built
# from the repository root — see its header).
#
# Two reasons something is listed here: it would bloat the context (node_modules and
# build output run to hundreds of megabytes, and the builder installs its own anyway),
# or it must never reach an image at all (env files, local databases, signing material).

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
out
**/out
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local configuration. `.env.example` is excluded alongside `.env` on
# purpose: `database/dataSource.ts` falls back to reading it, and its contents are
# LOCAL dev defaults (CLOUD_DEV_NO_AUTH=1, the sa password) that must never be
# available to fall back to in a deployed container.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*

# The desktop app's local databases and any stray copies.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite

# Version control, editor and CI metadata — nothing in the image reads them.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and desktop-only packaging inputs. apps/client is not part of the server
# image's dependency subtree, but excluding its heaviest inputs keeps the context small.
docs
apps/client/build
apps/client/dist
**/*.md
!README.md

# Test artefacts and scratch space.
coverage
**/coverage
